  "source_text": "Title: Caramelized Onion Hummus\nServings: 4\n\nIngredients (component | amount unit | name | prep_style | pantry food_id):\n- Caramelized Onions | 200 g | onion |  | 000111\n- Caramelized Onions | 15 g | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Caramelized Onions | 2 g | sea salt |  | 000294\n- Hummus Base | 400 g | chickpeas |  | 000061\n- Hummus Base | 60 g | seed butters (tahini) |  | 000408\n- Hummus Base | 50 g | lemon |  | 000130\n- Hummus Base | 10 g | garlic |  | 000112\n- Hummus Base | 30 g | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Hummus Base | 3 g | sea salt |  | 000294\n- Assembly and Garnish | 2 g | smoked paprika |  | 000291\n- Assembly and Garnish | 5 g | dill |  | 000249\n- Assembly and Garnish | 10 g | olive oil |  | 000378\n\nSteps in order (component | phase | minutes | text):\n1. Caramelized Onions | Prep |  | Peel and thinly slice the onions into uniform rounds or half-moons.\n2. Caramelized Onions | Cook |  | Heat 15g of olive oil in a pan over medium-low heat. Add onions and a pinch of salt, cooking for 25-30 minutes, stirring occasionally until deep golden brown and jammy.\n3. Hummus Base | Prep |  | Drain and rinse the chickpeas. Peel the garlic cloves and juice the lemon.\n4. Hummus Base | Cook |  | Place chickpeas, tahini, garlic, lemon juice, and salt in a food processor. Blitz until thick, then slowly drizzle in 30g of olive oil while processing until the hummus is perfectly smooth.\n5. Assembly and Garnish | Serve |  | Spoon the hummus onto a wide plate and use the back of a spoon to create a deep swirl. Top with the warm caramelized onions, a dusting of smoked paprika, fresh dill, and a final drizzle of olive oil.",
